                                <comments>
                            <comment id="17073703" author="alex_pl" created="Thu, 2 Apr 2020 12:52:39 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=akalashnikov&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;akalashnikov&quot;&gt;akalashnikov&lt;/a&gt;, could you please review the patch? It&apos;s related to &lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/IGNITE-12593&quot; title=&quot;Corruption of B+Tree caused by byte array values and TTL&quot; class=&quot;issue-link&quot; data-issue-key=&quot;IGNITE-12593&quot;&gt;&lt;del&gt;IGNITE-12593&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt;, which you have been fixed recently.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="17073865" author="ignitetcbot" created="Thu, 2 Apr 2020 16:19:04 +0000"  >&lt;div class=&quot;panel&quot; style=&quot;border-color: #ccc;border-style: dashed;border-width: 1px;&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;panelHeader&quot; style=&quot;border-bottom-width: 1px;border-bottom-style: dashed;border-bottom-color: #ccc;background-color: #D6F7C1;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Branch: &lt;span class=&quot;error&quot;&gt;&amp;#91;pull/7609/head&amp;#93;&lt;/span&gt; Base: &lt;span class=&quot;error&quot;&gt;&amp;#91;master&amp;#93;&lt;/span&gt; : No blockers found!&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://ci.ignite.apache.org/viewLog.html?buildId=5182438&amp;amp;buildTypeId=IgniteTests24Java8_RunAll&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;TeamCity &lt;b&gt;--&amp;gt; Run :: All&lt;/b&gt; Results&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="17083192" author="akalashnikov" created="Tue, 14 Apr 2020 12:58:07 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=alex_pl&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;alex_pl&quot;&gt;alex_pl&lt;/a&gt; &lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=alex_pl&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;alex_pl&quot;&gt;alex_pl&lt;/a&gt; thanks for your changes. But unfortunately, it broke one important invariant. &lt;br/&gt;
There was a bug with deadlock between checkpointLock and entryLock - they were taken in a different order in different cases. It was fixed at &lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/IGNITE-12594&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow&quot;&gt;https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/IGNITE-12594&lt;/a&gt;, so after that, we always take entryLock only after checkpointLock. These changes weren&apos;t clear enough because they require from you invoking method such GridCacheMapEntry#innerGet only under checkpointLock which is not obvious. Anyway, as I can see your changes make it possible to reorder these locks again, which is not good and it should be fixed. If you have an idea of how to simplify lock ordering logic, please, share it. &lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="17089380" author="alex_pl" created="Wed, 22 Apr 2020 07:25:33 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=akalashnikov&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;akalashnikov&quot;&gt;akalashnikov&lt;/a&gt;&#160;I&apos;ve made fixes taking into account &lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/IGNITE-12594&quot; title=&quot;Deadlock between GridCacheDataStore#purgeExpiredInternal and GridNearTxLocal#enlistWriteEntry&quot; class=&quot;issue-link&quot; data-issue-key=&quot;IGNITE-12594&quot;&gt;&lt;del&gt;IGNITE-12594&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt;. Please have a look again.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="17089381" author="ignitetcbot" created="Wed, 22 Apr 2020 07:25:46 +0000"  >&lt;div class=&quot;panel&quot; style=&quot;border-color: #ccc;border-style: dashed;border-width: 1px;&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;panelHeader&quot; style=&quot;border-bottom-width: 1px;border-bottom-style: dashed;border-bottom-color: #ccc;background-color: #D6F7C1;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Branch: &lt;span class=&quot;error&quot;&gt;&amp;#91;pull/7609/head&amp;#93;&lt;/span&gt; Base: &lt;span class=&quot;error&quot;&gt;&amp;#91;master&amp;#93;&lt;/span&gt; : No blockers found!&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://ci.ignite.apache.org/viewLog.html?buildId=5246488&amp;amp;buildTypeId=IgniteTests24Java8_RunAll&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;TeamCity &lt;b&gt;--&amp;gt; Run :: All&lt;/b&gt; Results&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="17090458" author="alex_pl" created="Thu, 23 Apr 2020 10:04:50 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;To solve the problem checkpoint read lock is added for the&#160;&lt;tt&gt;get&lt;/tt&gt;&#160;operation to each cache adapter except near cache adapters (near cache entries have no-op &lt;tt&gt;removeValue()&lt;/tt&gt;&#160;and &lt;tt&gt;mvccRemoveAll()&lt;/tt&gt;&#160;implementations and don&apos;t change page memory)&#160;&#160;&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="17094328" author="akalashnikov" created="Tue, 28 Apr 2020 09:23:39 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=alex_pl&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;alex_pl&quot;&gt;alex_pl&lt;/a&gt; Now it looks good to me. Thanks.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="17094338" author="alex_pl" created="Tue, 28 Apr 2020 09:43:28 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=akalashnikov&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;akalashnikov&quot;&gt;akalashnikov&lt;/a&gt;&#160;thank you for the review!&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Merged to master.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="17096301" author="alex_pl" created="Thu, 30 Apr 2020 08:23:53 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Cherry-picked to 2.8.1&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
